Their nostrils closed to keep them from, you know, suffocating in sand.

224
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Their eyelashes are long to, so that they could be able to see like all, like you just look at a camel.

225
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:27,000
I can imagine David just looking at a camel and saying, that doesn't happen by accident.

226
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:35,000
That strange looking animal with a massive hump on his back was created by a all wise God to survive in this place.

227
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:44,000
So that we can travel and we can do the things we need to be, to do to thrive.

228
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:53,000
From some of the smallest to some of the largest animals that David could observe, he could clearly see God's wisdom in his handiwork.

229
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:58,000
And we have the privilege of learning from a guy like David who spent all of his time outside.

230
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:08,000
And we have the privilege of learning from modern science who has been able to explore the universe far, far more than David ever would have.

231
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:18,000
And scientists talk about this thing the earth exists in called the habitable, habitable zone, there we go.

232
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:25,000
For those of you that got like a C minus in science, like me, the Goldilocks zone, right?

233
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,000
We've heard it like that, that I resonate with.

234
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:39,000
It's this place in which it's very, very rare for a planet like ours to be positioned where it is so that it can have all of the necessities of life.

235
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:43,000
It's incredibly rare for a planet like earth to be positioned where it is to give us all, I just said that.

236
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
I told you I wrote this a week ago.

237
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Here you go, you got it twice.

238
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:52,000
God's creation, it clearly communicates his wisdom to us.

239
00:17:53,000 --> 00:18:00,000
From the smallest plants and animals to the structure of the galaxy, God's wisdom can be seen throughout all creation.

240
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:12,000
And as we zoom out from the smallest animal to the largest universes that we can observe, it starts, it begins to bring God's power into clarity.

241
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:15,000
The immensity of creation shows God's power.

242
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:22,000
I'll never forget the first night, Marissa and I moved into our house in Virginia, for those of you who have been there.

243
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
We live in the middle of nowhere.

244
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
And it is awesome.

245
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:34,000
But we were moving from the city of Wilkes-Barre, which is not a huge city, but it's definitely a city.

246
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:39,000
You know, we were on the corner of a block, there's lights and there's stuff everywhere.

247
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:47,000
We moved to Gore, Virginia in the middle of nowhere in the fall and I just walked out under the night sky.

248
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:55,000
I heard the wind blowing through these large palm trees that are out of the corner of my yard and I looked up at the sky and I'd never seen a sky so beautiful.

249
00:18:55,000 --> 00:19:03,000
The power of God, the immensity of God's creation.

250
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,000
And David takes it a step further.

251
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Not only does he acknowledge how powerful God is through the skies, but he corrects the theology of many people of his day.

252
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:21,000
He talks about how the sun is just eager to obey the word of God.

253
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:27,000
The sun, the most powerful, incredible thing that they might have ever even observed or thought of.

254
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:34,000
They were tempted, cultures all around David were tempted to worship the sun as a God or the God itself.

255
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:44,000
And David says, no, no, no, no, God is so powerful that that thing that you think is the most powerful thing that you could ever imagine is eager to obey God daily.

256
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:50,000
It does what he tells it to do because our God is powerful.

257
00:19:50,000 --> 00:20:06,000
And the same could be said, you know, I was thinking about that this week and you're like, all right, Ryan, but like people these days aren't that clueless, right?

258
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
People aren't worshiping the sun.

259
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:16,000
But if we think about the ideology of atheistic scientists, that's what they're doing.

260
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:24,000
They're looking at the incredible nature of creation, the power of creation, and they're attributing the power of creation to creation itself.

261
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,000
The creation somehow just figured out how to do this.

262
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:39,000
And I am not anti-science, we can learn an incredible amount from science, but if we're gonna learn from science, we have to start with the fact that creation does what God tells it to do.

263
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:43,000
The sun does what God tells it to do.

264
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:51,000
And if we begin to attribute worth and worship and honor and glory to creation itself, we've missed the point entirely.

265
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:59,000
David says, creation clearly communicates God's wisdom, his power, and his beauty.

266
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:04,000
All of this adds up to creation, revealing God's beauty or his glory all four seasons.

267
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:17,000
From continent to continent, from desert plains to the Arctic tundra, from the remote rainforest to the urban center, all of creation is clearly communicating God's wisdom and his power and his beauty.

268
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
So much so that we can get a glimpse into the heavenly realm.

269
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:23,000
When we get a glimpse into the heavenly realm.

270
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:37,000
When we get a glimpse into the heavenly realm, in the book of Revelation, we hear this chorus of praise breaking out.

271
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:41,000
You are worthy, O Lord our God, to receive glory and honor and power.

272
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Why?

273
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:47,000
For you created all things and they exist because you created what you please.

274
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:54,000
This is the heavenly beings breaking out in the praise chorus that David wrote.

275
00:21:54,000 --> 00:22:02,000
In his time, in his space, the same praise chorus is being sung throughout all creation for all eternity by the heavenly beings around the throne.

276
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:07,000
You are worthy to receive honor and power and glory because of what you have made.

277
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:13,000
Just look around at the glorious manifestation of your presence in creation.

278
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:19,000
So the question then becomes, are we listening?

279
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Are we receiving God's communication about himself through nature?

280
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:30,000
We regularly take time to reflect on the wisdom, power, and beauty found in God's creation.

281
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:35,000
And when we see the brokenness of creation, because can we all acknowledge that creation is broken?

282
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:51,000
This psalm invites us to wrestle with, when we come in contact with the brokenness of creation, are we going to attribute the brokenness of creation to the God who created it with wisdom, power, and beauty?

283
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:58,000
Or are we going to acknowledge that it is us who has broken creation?

284
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:06,000
And this is one of the most difficult realities that I wrestle with with people on a regular basis, is they are faced with the brokenness of creation.

285
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Is the natural tendency is to jump to God.

286
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,000
How could God let this happen?

287
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Why did God do this?

288
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Why is God doing this?

289
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Why is God doing this?

290
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:23,000
And I think this psalm helps us to realize that creation as it is intended to be, is wise, powerful, and beautiful.

291
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
And it's still, we can still see it.

292
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:29,000
And yet when we see the brokenness, we cannot attribute the brokenness to God.

293
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Because we are the ones that rebelled against God.

294
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:41,000
So are we listening and are we communicating through God's creation?

295
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:45,000
We are created in God's image and we are invited to have dominion over his creation.

296
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:52,000
Are we having dominion in such a way that reflects his wisdom, his power, and his beauty or our own selfish desire?

297
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:59,000
This is, I don't know how much to get into this a little bit.

298
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:07,000
Just a prophetic announcement, not against us as individuals, but against our society as a whole.

299
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:16,000
I am committed now and I don't know if I want it to or not.

300
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:32,000
The way in which we as individuals and we as larger corporations interact with the creation that God has given us.

301
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Do we do it in a way that is all about how we can be profitable in this small, ample period of time?

302
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Or do we zoom out and say this is a gift from God to be stewarded?

303
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:51,000
And again, I say this because most of us don't have the power to make the decisions that are being made with God's creation in this way.

304
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:56,000
But we can, as individuals, what are we doing?

305
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:04,000
To communicate to the world around us that God has given us a gift and this gift is to be stewarded for the good of everyone.

306
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:07,000
Not just for our own selfish ambition.

307
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Ambition.

308
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:14,000
God's creation is wisdom, power, it's beauty.

309
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,000
And it goes beyond all geography and all culture and all language.

310
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,000
It's hard to misinterpret.

311
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:24,000
God is not just speaking to one category of people, to one culture of people, to one language of people.

312
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:29,000
When he offers creation as his love language to the world, it is to the whole world.

313
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:38,000
So that everyone can see and be without excuse that there is a God who is wise and powerful and beautiful.

314
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:47,000
He moves on because what we find out throughout Scripture is that this isn't all that God wants us to know about himself.

315
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:54,000
What we can learn through creation is like God, character, and love 101.

316
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Right?

317
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:57,000
But he offers us 201.

318
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:00,000
It isn't all that God wants to communicate about himself.

319
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:09,000
So God enters a specific culture and a specific language and communicates more clearly to us through his law.

320
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Specifically through the law of the people of Israel.

321
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Let's read it in verse seven.

322
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:20,000
David says, "The law of the Lord is perfect, refreshing the soul.

323
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:24,000
The statutes of the Lord are trustworthy, making the wise simple.

324
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:27,000
The precepts of the Lord are right, giving joy to the heart.

325
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:31,000
The commands of the Lord are radiant, giving light to the eyes.

326
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:35,000
The fear of the Lord is pure, enduring forever.

327
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:37,000
The decrees of the Lord are firm.

328
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:40,000
And all of them are righteous.

329
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:45,000
They are more precious than gold, more than pure gold.

330
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:48,000
They are sweeter than honey, honey from the honeycomb.

331
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:53,000
By them your servant is warned in keeping them.

332
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:55,000
There is great reward."

333
00:26:55,000 --> 00:27:07,000
David switches here from the general term for God, which is El, to the specific name of God that he gave to the Israel people, which is Yahweh.

334
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:16,000
It's almost like David wants us to see and to acknowledge that God's written word gives us a clearer definition of who he is than just his creation.

335
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:25,000
That God is drawing closer to us, that he is giving us more specific understanding of who he is, more than can just be observed in creation.

336
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:28,000
God doesn't just give us creation and hope we figure it out.

337
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
He moves closer.

338
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:36,000
It's what he has been doing since our rebellion in the garden.

339
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,000
It's what he continues to do.

340
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:39,000
God moves closer to us.

341
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:43,000
He gives us clearer definitions of who he is.

342
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:47,000
He chooses to specifically inhabit the people, the culture, and the language of Israel.

343
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Not because Israel is better than any other people, culture, or language, but because of his grace.

344
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,000
I need us to hear that.

345
00:27:55,000 --> 00:28:01,000
God chose to work through the nation of Israel, not because they were special, but because he is gracious.

346
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:15,000
And he chose to move into a specific people, group, culture, and language so that every tribe, nation, and tongue could hear and see and have the word of God translated into their language and the gospel of Jesus given to them in their language.

347
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:19,000
In their language, God is moving closer to us.

348
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:24,000
He is giving us the clearer definition of who he is through his word.

349
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:35,000
As I pondered this, again, beautiful and poetic language about God's law, his written word, I summarized it this way.

350
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:42,000
God's word is good, and it is intended to enlighten, encourage, and convict.

351
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:45,000
I mean, just read it, there's adjectives and verbs.

352
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:50,000
It's all just like it's saying the same thing over and over and over again, that God's word is perfect.

353
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:52,000
It brings benefit to us.

354
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:55,000
God's statutes are trustworthy, it brings benefit to us.

355
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,000
His precepts are right, it brings benefit to us.

356
00:28:57,000 --> 00:29:03,000
God's word is given to us so that we might live the abundant life that he created us for.

357
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:05,000
But are we listening?

358
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:08,000
Are we receiving it as good?

359
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Are we allowing it to enlighten, encourage, and convict us?

360
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:22,000
And I know what some of you might be thinking, especially since all that David has when he's writing this is the Old Testament.

361
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Anybody know where I'm going with this?

362
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:39,000
I know what some of you might be thinking, "Pastor, I've read the Old Testament, and there's some stuff in there that doesn't seem good, and it doesn't do too much to enlighten or encourage me."

363
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:44,000
And I just want to acknowledge that tension this morning, and I want you to know that I hear you and that I resonate with you.

364
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:54,000
I'm in the Old Testament right now in my reading through the Bible in a year plan, and there's some passages where I'm like, good, enlightening, encouraging, like, ah, I'm struggling.

365
00:29:54,000 --> 00:30:01,000
But I think that it's important that we zoom out and make sure we get the big picture before we lose the forest for the trees.

366
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:11,000
When God is giving the very beginning of His law, the Ten Commandments to Moses on Mount Sinai, the second time, right?

367
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:20,000
The second time, which again demonstrates God's graciousness and faithfulness to a people who is rebellious and unfaithful to the thing that He's inviting them to.

368
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:25,000
Again, we often look at God and we're like, "Where's the goodness? Where's the encouragement?"

369
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:28,000
It's like, ah, mirror? Anybody?

370
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Okay, so when God was giving His people the law the second time, He tells Moses essentially a two-sentence summary of God's character.

371
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:44,000
He's like, "If you want to know who I am, this is who I am."

372
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:49,000
In my opinion, my humble opinion, one of the most significant passages in the entire Bible, Yahweh,

373
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:55,000
Yahweh, the Creator God who is wise and beautiful and powerful, He draws near to a specific group of person,

374
00:30:55,000 --> 00:31:00,000
to an individual who is broken, imperfect, and messed up, and He draws near to Him.

375
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
And He says this, "The Lord came down in a cloud and He stood there with Moses."

376
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:09,000
He called out His own personal name to Moses.

377
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:15,000
He said, "Yahweh, the Lord, the God of compassion and mercy.

378
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:23,000
I am slow to anger and I am filled with unfailing love and faithfulness."

379
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:30,000
God's summary statement about Himself to His people, "This is who I am."

380
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:34,000
I lavish unfailing love to a thousand generations.

381
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:40,000
I forgive iniquity, rebellion, and sins, but I do not excuse the guilty.

382
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:47,000
And what I get from this passage is that all of God's word is aimed at helping us better understand this God

383
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:53,000
in His abounding steadfast love.

384
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:55,000
But He's not holding anything back from us, right?

385
00:31:55,000 --> 00:32:00,000
He also says, "I am just and I will not let unchecked, unrepentant sin go unpunished

386
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:04,000
because unchecked and unrepentant sin causes harm to ourselves and others."

387
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:09,000
And I am a God who is gracious and compassionate and I do not want you to harm yourself or others.

388
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:13,000
And so I will be just if you continue to plug your ears and close your eyes

389
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:17,000
and do whatever it is that you want to do without my permission."

390
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:21,000
So when we come to a passage of Scripture that doesn't seem to be good,

391
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:26,000
that doesn't enlighten, encourage, or convict us according to God's definition of Himself,

392
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:30,000
then my argument is that we are missing something and we should keep digging.

393
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:34,000
And this is a lifelong pursuit.

394
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:38,000
I've been studying the Scripture pretty seriously for a number of years

395
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:43,000
and there are still some really difficult passages where I have yet to find where it is good,

396
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:45,000
enlightening, encouraging, and convicting.

397
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:49,000
But I just trust Yahweh enough.

398
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:53,000
I've lived enough life with this God who is compassionate and gracious,

399
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:55,000
slow to anger, abounding in steadfast love.

400
00:32:55,000 --> 00:33:00,000
I've done enough life with Him that I can trust Him in the tension of the difficulty of the passages

401
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:02,000
that I have come to not yet understand.

402
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:05,000
And I hope this testimony is an encouragement to you.

403
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:11,000
When you come to a difficult passage, when you don't understand what it is that God is doing, keep wrestling.

404
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:18,000
One of the fathers of the nation of Israel, like he's famous for wrestling with God.

405
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:24,000
The Jewish people still to this day, they cling to that when they wrestle in the text of Scripture.

406
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:28,000
They never want to just read it and say, okay, God said it, I believe it, we're moving on.

407
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:34,000
No, they wrestle with God and we as a people of God are invited to wrestle with God when we struggle.

408
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:51,000
And I think so many people have walked away from the faith because people on stages like this have read complex, difficult passages of Scripture and tried to make them simple and say, believe it, get over your struggles and move on.

409
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:54,000
And people haven't been able to do that.

410
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:57,000
And what I want to create here at our church is a culture where it's okay to wrestle.

411
00:33:57,000 --> 00:34:01,000
It's okay to not understand.

412
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:05,000
But we fall back on the definition of God he gives to us.

413
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:09,000
He is compassionate and gracious, slow to anger, abounding, steadfast, love.

414
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:11,000
You guys alive?

415
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:13,000
Okay.

416
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:19,000
I lost my place because I said a lot of things that weren't in my notes.

417
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:20,000
There we go.

418
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:33,000
Marissa and I regularly have discussions about what type of rules we are going to implement with Rory as he gets older and gains more independence.

419
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Rules about screen time, devices, social media, sleepovers, you know, these type of things that are going to be challenging and difficult.

420
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:52,000
And our theory is that if we pre-decide now, before he comes to us and says, but my friends, but my friends, it's like, if we can get on the same page now, write some declarations down, get ahead of it.

421
00:34:52,000 --> 00:35:01,000
That maybe we will be able to stay steadfast in the midst of his, you know, loving face.

422
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,000
I know you guys are laughing at me.

423
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:04,000
All of you that have older kids, you're like, good luck.

424
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:15,000
Hey, right now it might be pie in the sky, but we're still, we're, we're convinced that we'll be able to do it by God's grace.

425
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:21,000
And in 10 years, when we mess up, I'll, I'll look to you all and you can tell me, you can tell me what to do next.

426
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:25,000
But here's the reality about that.

427
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Is no matter how poorly we executed, I know for a fact that there are going to be some or many rules that will be interpreted by Rory's friends as unkind, unloving, or at least, at the very least, unfun.

428
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:55,000
But my hope and my prayer is that because of the time and relationship invested in my beautiful baby boy,

429
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:59,000
that when he comes to a rule that he doesn't understand,

430
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:05,000
when he comes to a decree that me and his mother have made that is for his good,

431
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:15,000
that even if he can't see it, and even if he doesn't understand it, and even if everyone around him and all his friends are saying, your parents stink.

432
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:19,000
They don't want you to have fun.

433
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:22,000
They don't want you to experience true and abundant life.

434
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:31,000
My hope and my prayer is that he will look at his mother and his father who have loved him, who have loved him well.

435
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:34,000
And he will say, I don't get this one.

436
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:37,000
This one doesn't make any sense to me.

437
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:40,000
But I trust him.

438
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:53,000
My hope is that because of Rory's relational proximity to us, that even if he doesn't understand every rule we put into place,

439
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:58,000
that ultimately he will choose to submit to them because of our relationship and track record of sacrificial love.

440
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:02,000
And I think that's what David is expressing here in this poem.

441
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:06,000
I don't think David fully understood all of God's decrees and all of his laws.

442
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:11,000
And we might not fully understand why God says or does what he says or does in every situation.

443
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:19,000
But for those of us who have had a track record of relationship with him, who have seen his faithfulness and his grace to us and others,

444
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:24,000
my prayer is that we can with conviction say that the law of the Lord is perfect.

445
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:30,000
Refreshing the soul, the statutes of the Lord are trustworthy, making wise the simple.

446
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:34,000
The precepts of the Lord are right, giving joy to the heart.

447
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:38,000
The commands of the Lord are radiant, giving light to the eyes.

448
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:41,000
The fear of the Lord is pure, enduring forever.

449
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:47,000
The decrees of the Lord are firm and all of them are righteous.

450
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:54,000
They are more precious than gold, much more than pure gold.

451
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:57,000
They are sweeter than honey from the honeycomb.

452
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:04,000
When we interact with God's word, does it enlighten and convict and encourage us?

453
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:05,000
Do we view it as good?

454
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:09,000
And when we communicate God's word to others,

455
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:15,000
do we do so in a way that enlightens, encourages and convicts?

456
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:20,000
If not, we are presenting a shallow or false version of God to those around us.

457
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:22,000
And I don't have time to get into it a bunch.

458
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:25,000
I can just give you a couple hints and you'll know.

459
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:32,000
But there are categories of Christians that only want to share things about God that encourage.

460
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:46,000
And what I'm going to stand on in my leadership of this church is that we have to be a people that share all of it.

461
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:50,000
That we have to be encouraging.

462
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:55,000
We have to meet people where they are and speak the love of God into their life.

463
00:38:56,000 --> 00:39:02,000
And yet we have to stand firm on truth when God says things that we don't even understand, that don't make sense to us.

464
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:04,000
And we're like, God, why this rule?

465
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:10,000
That we're willing to trust him and invite others to trust him in the same way.

466
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:21,000
David moves from understanding God's language of creation, his language and his word, and this leads him to some time of self-reflection.

467
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:28,000
He allows God's revelation about himself through creation and through his word to lead him to some self-reflection.

468
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:36,000
I heard one pastor say that this passage invites us to look up at God's creation, to look down at God's word, and to look in at our own hearts.

469
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:39,000
Verse 12.

470
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:43,000
But who can discern their own errors?

471
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Forgive me, God, for my hidden faults.

472
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:51,000
Keep your servant also from willful sins.

473
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:53,000
May they not rule over me.

474
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:57,000
Then I will be blameless and innocent of great transgression.

475
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:59,000
He ends with this incredible prayer of reflection.

476
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:06,000
May these words of my mouth and the meditations of my heart be pleasing in your sight, Lord, my rock and my redeemer.

477
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Because God has made his wisdom, his power and his beauty known to us through creation, because his word enlightens, encourages and convicts, we should surrender our lives to his leadership.

478
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:25,000
That's what David is wrestling with here in this last section.

479
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:30,000
But he knows firsthand experience that it isn't as easy as it sounds in a poem.

480
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:33,000
We are broken people.

481
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:38,000
So David says here, God, I sin and I don't even realize that I'm sinning.

482
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:41,000
Reveal that to me.

483
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:45,000
Show me the ways in which I am rebelling against you without my knowledge.

484
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:50,000
Forgive me of that and give me the ability to quit it.

485
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:56,000
And then he moves on and he says, and then there's some sins like that I know for a fact are sins and I keep doing it.

486
00:40:56,000 --> 00:41:02,000
Any of us?

487
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:07,000
Any of us so broken, so rebellion that we're sinning and we don't even realize it?

488
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:16,000
Any of us so stubborn that we know we're sinning and we keep doing it even though we know it's killing us and those around us?

489
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:24,000
What David comes to reflect on, he says, God, may the meditations of my heart, may the words of my mouth be pleasing to you.

490
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:27,000
May I realize the sins that I'm committing that I don't know about.

491
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:33,000
And may I repent and have victory over the sins that I do know about.

492
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:38,000
God's word and his creation should lead us to some self-reflection.

493
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:49,000
God's word and his creation should lead us to some repentance.
